From: Codex <codex@openai.local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:24:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] A measured ceiling of zero is the midnight race, not a day
 with no budget

CAUGHT LIVE ON THE TRADING BOX, 2026-09-25 at 00:00:03 UTC, and it had the whole day's research
in it.

An organ made a free call three seconds into the new UTC day. The desk's spend ledger had no rows
for the new date yet, so `calls_today()` was 0. OpenRouter's own daily counter had NOT rolled --
the 429 body carried `X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0` with a reset stamp still in the future -- so the
call was refused. `note_free_limit_hit` recorded that refusal faithfully, at the count it saw:
`{"date": "2026-09-25", "ceiling": 0}`. `free_daily_max()` then returned min(900, 0) = 0.

FROM THAT MOMENT THE DESK REFUSED ITSELF. `free_budget_left()` returned 0, so every organ was
turned away by `chat()` BEFORE any HTTP request was made, for twenty-four hours, with
"free-tier daily request budget exhausted: 0 call(s) today against a 0 ceiling" -- a message that
reads exactly like a provider limit. Measured eleven minutes later, the provider said
`free_model_daily_requests: {used: 13, limit: 1000, remaining: 987}`. The budget was entirely
available and the desk could not see it.

This is the whole novel-mechanism lane. A mechanism with no registered family function reaches
the gauntlet only through an exact-rule extraction, and every extraction is one of those
requests, so a day pinned at zero is a day with no possibility of discovering anything the desk
did not already know. It would have recurred every night the previous day ended exhausted --
which, at 1,008 of 1,000 requests used, is every night.

ZERO COMPLETIONS IS NOT EVIDENCE ABOUT TODAY. It says the refusal arrived before this desk had
successfully called anything, which is a fact about YESTERDAY's exhaustion observed through a
counter that had not yet rolled. So it is UNMEASURED rather than zero (L1.28a) and the configured
default governs. If the provider really is still refusing, the next call takes its own 429 and
records a ceiling that means something.

`free_daily_max()` also floors at 1 now. The configured path already had that law -- "a ceiling of
zero would be a permanently dark desk", which is why QUANT_FREE_DAILY_MAX=0 floors at one -- and
the measured path reached the same dark desk by a different road. Belt to that brace, so a later
change reintroducing a zero from anywhere still cannot take the seat out for a day.

FOUND BY THE EXPERIMENT RATHER THAN BY READING. A four-arm A/B was queued to settle whether the
58% "reply was not a JSON object" loss is truncation; all 48 calls came back refused, and the
refusal named its own cause. The probe cost nothing and paid for itself before measuring the
thing it was built for.

Verified on the box after the change: free_budget_left() 0 -> 900, provider remaining 981.

